silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_01_functors_as_typed_cross_kg_mappings_sections_02_vetclinic_kg_as_target_category_concrete_anchor#clinicalbodymassquality silm:hasLongDescription "The ClinicalBodyMassQuality is the clinic's standard body-mass quality, scaled in kilograms, used uniformly for every patient. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'ClinicalBodyMassQuality', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
